# Without this, COPY drags the host's tree into the image and quietly undoes what the
# Dockerfile works hard at.
#
# packages/wasm/vendor is deliberately NOT excluded any more, and that is the point of
# it being a submodule. It used to be: the wasm stage cloned at pinned SHAs, then
# `COPY packages/wasm ./` merged the host's unpinned copy on top - after the digest
# check had run - and build.sh skips a fetch when the directory is already there, so
# what got compiled into the miner every visitor runs was whatever was on the builder's
# disk. Excluding it was the workaround. Now the content in the context is pinned by the
# commit this repository records, so copying it in is the safe thing rather than the
# hazard, and the builder has no unpinned copy to leak.
packages/wasm/build

# node_modules are symlinks into version-pinned .bun paths. Copied over a
# `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, they point at whatever the host last resolved -
# which is right until the lockfile moves, and then a dangling symlink at import time.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Built in the image (web stage), so a host build is stale by definition.
packages/web/dist
packages/web/public/mine-*

# The live database and its WAL. Never belonged in a build context.
data

.git
.env
